+Towards the end, the project names a developing framework: the Queer Free Energy Principle, or QFEP. Its central concern here is how models can remain open to revision while the lives and possibilities they leave out retain the means to act and answer back. The two ghosts bring a question to that work: what capacities should this world preserve when the relationship it was built to support is itself changing? The afterword returns to this proposal with the encounters behind us. It asks what they let us claim, where they complicate the argument, and what remains to be tried. The reader can reach that discussion with questions of their own.
 
 Our route is one arrangement of attention. Other objects stand beside it; other histories could change its order. What matters is that following it gives us enough understanding to begin making such changes, together or alone.
 
